qpsmtpd (1.02) unstable; urgency=medium

  Envelope addresses (MAIL FROM, RCPT TO) are now parsed strictly along the
  RFC 5321 grammar.  Some paths that earlier releases accepted are rejected
  with "syntax error", among them:

   - unquoted specials in the localpart, such as ", (, < or \
   - more than one unquoted @, e.g. <a@b@example.com>
   - control characters anywhere in the path
   - malformed address literals, e.g. an IPv4 octet above 255

  Third-party plugins should be checked: Qpsmtpd::Address->new() returns
  undef for an invalid path, and the user(), host() and address() setters
  croak instead of storing an invalid value.

  The SMTPUTF8 extension (RFC 6531) is new in this release and disabled by
  default via /etc/qpsmtpd/smtputf8; see README.Debian before enabling it.

 -- Andreas Erhard <erhard@wor.net>  Thu, 01 Oct 2026 22:28:27 +0200
